rien","s":6,"p":[6,6],"r":[32,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Deut. xxxii. 6."},{"id":"e6b2860b7218","b":"COL","v":"npnf.athanasius.de_decretis","w":"athanasius.de_decretis","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":6,"p":[6,6],"r":[1,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Col. i. 15, and Ps. cx. 3."},{"id":"53587a51c478","b":"PSA","v":"npnf.athanasius.de_decretis","w":"athanasius.de_decretis","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":6,"p":[6,6],"r":[110,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Col. i. 15, and Ps. cx. 3."},{"id":"c220226ba6d1","b":"PRO","v":"npnf.athanasius.de_decretis","w":"athanasius.de_decretis","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":6,"p":[6,6],"r":[8,25],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Prov. viii. 25."},{"id":"0f2e7ed6e069","b":"JHN","v":"npnf.athanasius.de_decretis","w":"athanasius.de_decretis","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":7,"p":[3,3],"r":[14,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"John xiv. 9, John xiv. 10."},{"id":"d91a3332ecfb","b":"JHN","v":"npnf.athanasius.de_decretis","w":"athanasius.de_decretis","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":7,"p":[3,3],"r":[14,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"John xiv. 9, John xiv. 10."},{"id":"e4424ca35659","b":"MAT","v":"npnf.athanasius.de_decretis","w":"athanasius.de_decretis","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":7,"p":[3,3],"r":[6,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Matt. vi. 9."},{"id":"32628beb8201","b":"JHN","v":"npnf.athanasius.de_decretis","w":"athanasius.de_decretis","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":7,"p":[3,3],"r":[1,12,1,27],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"uiopoioumeqa alhqwj . This strong term `truly' or `verily' seems taken from such passages as speak of the `grace and truth' of the Gospel, John i. 12-27. Again S. Basil says, that we are sons, kuriwj , `properly,' and prwtwj `primarily,' in opposition to tropikwj fusikwj as well as kata xarin uioj . i. 3. Of these words, alhqwj, fusikwj, kuriwj , and prwtwj , the first two are commonly reserved for our Lord; e.g. ton alhqwj uion hmeij uioi, ouk wj ekeinoj fusei kai alhqeia idion , not kuriwj . And when Justin says of Christ o monoj legomenoj kuriwj uioj kuriwj seems to be used in reference to the word kurioj , Lord, which he has just been using, kuriologein being sometimes used by him as others in the sense of `naming as Lord,' like qeologein egw eimi o wn , uses the word in the same ambiguous sense; ouden gar onoma epi qeou kuriologeisqai dunaton , 21; as if kurioj fusikwj kuriwtaton dia paqouj idioj uioj and monogenhj , which are in Scripture, and the symbols `of the essence,' and `one in essence,' of the Council; and this is the value of the Council's phrases, that, while they guard the Son's divinity, they allow full scope, without risk of entrenching on it, to the Catholic doctrine of the fulness of the Christian privileges. vid. supr. §19, note."},{"id":"36f9afca95d9","b":"GAL","v":"npnf.athanasius.de_decretis","w":"athanasius.de_decretis","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":7,"p":[3,3],"r":[4,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gal. iv. 6."},{"id":"a7faa90d066c","b":"JER","v":"npnf.athanasius.de_decretis","w":"athanasius.de_decretis","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":7,"p":[4,4],"r":[13,23],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Jer. xiii. 23."}]}
